{# Flash messages for every dashboard page, rendered once by the layout.

   This used to be a block copy-pasted into individual page templates, so
   whether a confirmation appeared depended on which page the controller
   happened to redirect to. Six templates had the block; every page added since
   did not — and the controllers redirecting *there* had their message dropped
   in silence. "DMARC policy published: p=quarantine", "Note saved.",
   "Sender authorized.", "Released quarantined reports for X." and the whole of
   billing reached nobody. Owning it in the layout means a new page cannot
   forget, because it never has to remember.

   `rendered_elsewhere` types have a deliberate home of their own and are left
   alone. Peeking rather than reading the bag is what makes that possible:
   `app.flashes` with no argument CLEARS every type, so a generic loop here
   would swallow the messages those templates are waiting for. #}
{% set rendered_elsewhere = [
    'domain_recheck',
    'team_success',
    'team_error',
    'domain_taken_success',
    'domain_taken_error',
] %}

{% if app.request.hasSession %}
    {% for type, messages in app.session.flashBag.peekAll() %}
        {% if type not in rendered_elsewhere %}
            {# Unknown types are neutral, never alarming: a message we cannot
               classify is not evidence that something is wrong. #}
            {% set tone = {'error': 'error', 'warning': 'warning', 'success': 'success'}[type]|default('info') %}
            {% for message in app.flashes(type) %}
                <div class="alert alert-{{ tone }} mb-4" role="{{ 'error' == tone ? 'alert' : 'status' }}">
                    <span>{{ message }}</span>
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
{% endif %}
